Q1 – Building Text Under Load: String, StringBuilder or StringBuffer?
Bloom's Taxonomy: K4 – Analyse
Topic: Railway e-Ticket Generation
Marks: 6

1. Problem analysis and prediction
A railway reservation system generates e-tickets by combining several fields, including PNR, passenger name, coach, berth, fare and journey details.

Java provides three commonly used approaches:

String: Immutable. Every concatenation using + creates a new String result.

StringBuilder: Mutable. Appends text to the same internal character buffer, avoiding repeated intermediate String objects.

StringBuffer: Similar to StringBuilder, but its methods are synchronized, making individual operations thread-safe.

